%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e7a5919ff3dd728499db3d01b9c7d9c4, type: 3}
  m_Name: Level1InteractionSequence
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lines:
  - text: First let's check the Protocol and Flags... (Click on the first train compartment)
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 1
      allowedInteractionIds:
      - train_compartment1
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: In this train, the protocol is TCP and the flags are SYN, ACK.
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 0
      allowedInteractionIds: []
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: Nothing seems out of the ordinary, we're done here. (Close the window with
      the "x" at the top right)
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 1
      allowedInteractionIds:
      - close_train_compartment_popup
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: Next, let's check the Source IP/Port... (Click on the second train compartment)
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 1
      allowedInteractionIds:
      - train_compartment2
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: 'In this train, the source IP is 132.432.255.255 and the source port is
      443 '
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 0
      allowedInteractionIds: []
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: Nothing seems out of the ordinary, we're done here. (Close the window with
      the "x" at the top right)
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 1
      allowedInteractionIds:
      - close_train_compartment_popup
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: Next, let's check the Frame Number and Packet Size... (Click on the third
      train compartment)
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 1
      allowedInteractionIds:
      - train_compartment3
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: In this train, the Frame Number is 2 and the Packet Size is 70 bytes.
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 0
      allowedInteractionIds: []
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: Nothing seems out of the ordinary, we're done here. (Close the window with
      the "x" at the top right)
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 1
      allowedInteractionIds:
      - close_train_compartment_popup
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: Lastly, let's check the Payload... (Click on the fourth train compartment)
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 1
      allowedInteractionIds:
      - train_compartment4
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: This job doesn't pay us enough to decipher what's being passed in the payload
      of a TCP packet. This field will be more useful for other protocols later.
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 0
      allowedInteractionIds: []
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: Nothing seems out of the ordinary, we're done here. (Close the window with
      the "x" at the top right)
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 1
      allowedInteractionIds:
      - close_train_compartment_popup
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: This kind of information doesn't seem suspicious. Therefore, we will accept
      the train. (Click "Accept" at the top)
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 1
      allowedInteractionIds:
      - accept_train
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: Not all trains are safe to pass through this town. Some fools try to bypass
      our security with malicious information.
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 0
      allowedInteractionIds: []
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: I'm counting on you to stop them and reject their request before it harms
      the company. If you let too many go bye, you're fired.
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 0
      allowedInteractionIds: []
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: If you're unsure of what kind of information is safe to let through, check
      your manual. (Click "Manual" in the top left)
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 1
      allowedInteractionIds:
      - open_manual
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: In here, you can review what kind of information we expect to receive on
      these trains.
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 0
      allowedInteractionIds: []
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: As you get better, we'll allow more complex trains to come your way, and
      in turn more of your manual will be available.
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 0
      allowedInteractionIds: []
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: That's enough with the manual for now. (Click the "Close" button to close
      the manual)
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 1
      allowedInteractionIds:
      - close_manual
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: Remember, review your checklist to make sure you checked every possible
      thing those fools might try to do. (Click the "Checklist" button in the top
      left)
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 1
      allowedInteractionIds:
      - open_checklist
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: In the Checklist, you can see which ip's and ports we are expecting to
      hear from today. Make sure all packets you accept are company approved, we
      can't risk any evildoers compromising us.
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 0
      allowedInteractionIds: []
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: Once you're done reviewing, go ahead and close the checklist. (Click the
      "Close" button in the bottom left)
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 1
      allowedInteractionIds:
      - close_checklist
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
  - text: Alright, you're on your own now, partner. Let's see how you fare! Oh, and...
      try not to get fired on the first day, will ya?
    speakerName: Sheriff
    portrait: {fileID: -7307842283543146795, guid: 8e858e9d9926f124392468c068f061d7, type: 3}
    useCustomRevealSpeed: 0
    revealLettersPerSecond: 0
    interactionRequirement:
      enabled: 0
      allowedInteractionIds: []
      requiredInteractionCount: 1
